0 FILE triceratops.ldr
0 BRICK Triceratops 77985 reconstruction draft
0 Name: triceratops-v0.mpd
0 Evidence: current official 6649865.pdf pp.11-13, 136-137, 148; reviewed step candidates supersede the earlier draft shape/connection assumptions.
0 Steps 4-6 are display-base/rock formation parts, not the fossil skull. Step 278 has been rebuilt from 32056, 92907 and 2x61332; step279 counterpart mapping remains provisional.
0 Author: BRICK project
0 !BRICK_STATE {"schema_version":3,"status":"instruction_reconstruction_in_progress","model":"Triceratops fossil reconstruction","reference_set":"LEGO 77985","reference_url":"https://www.lego.com/cdn/product-assets/product.bi.core.pdf/6649865.pdf","manual_files":["6649865.pdf"],"progress_note":"Latest origin/main 8ca6bf3 reviewed. MPD has 161 physical instance records referenced from the root, including explicitly isolated local subassemblies. Steps 4–6 are the display base/rock and remain named separately from fossil-skull fragments. Steps 247/249/278 were corrected from latest inventory evidence; 18980 grid registration, 249 core/6141 port axes, and 278 internal link hole axes/pin intervals are checked. Step279 external transform remains withheld because the matching skull-side male feature has not been identified in the assembled local skull. Steps250–277 remain a set of local candidate fragments; 280–290 base branches remain independent with hinge/placement uncertainties. Steps291–292 add no pieces, and 294 plaque/minifigure are excluded. Instance records include provisional candidates and are not a completed product BOM.","piece_count":161,"unique_sale_skus":7,"listed_retail_parts_cost_cny":"0.95","cost_scope":"Not totaled; candidate mappings only.","target_dimensions_cm":{"length":null,"height":null,"width":null},"reference_geometry_bounds_cm":{"length":null,"height":null,"width":null},"support_count":0,"support_verification":"Not assessed.","validation":{"instruction_scope":"Current official 6649865.pdf. Step 4 18980-to-60474 grid registration checked; step249 two-plate/two-6541 core and 6141-to-side-hole axes recalculated; step278 liftarm/crossblock/pin axis and insertion spans recalculated. Step279 external docking transform withheld because a matching completed skull submodel and compatible receiver are absent from the current assembly geometry. Independent steps 250 onward remain represented as local candidate fragments; their unresolved transforms do not block this link check.","placements":"Step278 internal two-pin fit: official DAT centerlines have 0 LDU transverse residual and 20 LDU face spacing; the nominal 11214 pin sections span their 32140/32184 bores. Step247 6541 hole center [20,20,20], axis +Y, is coaxial with the free 32140 port and its adjoining face; the two 6577 candidates are stacked vertically below the 6541, not placed through the side hole. Step249 support holes are 20 LDU apart and their candidate 43093/62462 axes are aligned; actual pin depth and whether the second 6541 axis is parallel or orthogonal remain unresolved; the user retained both candidates. 32184 is provisionally skull-side and the remaining 32140 port torso-side, so the receiver is not required to align with both axes. Step279 has no parts in its callout; the required sockets must pre-exist on the body. Step280 base strip uses a 2x10 plate with a 50340 dual-finger hinge candidate across its end; step281 has paired 1x3 plates on adjacent rows. These are independent local coordinates and remain diagram-based pending later platform stages. Official candidate port calculations: step249 6541 axes are both +Z and 20 LDU apart; each 43093 and the near hole of each 62462 are coaxial. The currently modeled far sockets are [390,-14,50] and [410,-14,50], both +Z. Step278 link has two remaining external candidates with +Y and +Z axes; the step278 ports now have separate provisional roles: 32184 toward the skull and the remaining 32140 hole toward the torso, following step279 docking order. Therefore the torso receiver need not fit both orthogonal axes. Keep the step249 parallel/orthogonal axis question local and unresolved; do not reject its candidate from a two-port mismatch alone. Step282 tile 2x4 is placed over the hinge-end studs as a diagram-based provisional cover. Step283 candidate rows use two official DAT height registrations: 3023b row at 8 LDU, 3700 row at 24 LDU, with 50340 plates stacked at the corresponding top levels. Finger direction and exact rows remain provisional. Step284 adds one 3021 2x3 plate and one 3022 2x2 plate to the independent base; IDs and official DAT shapes are registered, while exact overlap/row remain provisional. Step285 adds two 1762 double-curved slope shape candidates based on callout curvature and count; exact ID/orientation and stud footprint remain unverified. Step286 places one 30355/30356 mirrored 6x12-wing shape candidate on either side of the base; footprint and scale follow the manual, but mold allocation, hinge contact and engagement height remain tentative. Step287 adds one 67142/68196 left/right panel candidate based on four-hole pattern and tapered silhouette. Local long-axis alignment and edge offset are provisional; pin-axis engagement/depth not yet resolved. Step288 places two 24299 left-shape and two 24307 right-shape candidates, following the separate official left/right mold forms and 2x callouts; exact face, orientation and contact with the perforated panels remain provisional. Step289 independent branch begins with a 3666 1x6 plate and 3020 2x4 plate. Four stud centers align at 20-LDU pitch and vertical layer uses an 8-LDU plate offset; final attachment to the platform is withheld. Step289 substeps 3–5 continue the local independent branch with a 3023b plate, 50340 hinge candidate, 77850 rounded-end 1x3 candidate and 4032a round 2x2 candidate. Their local stack direction is diagram-based provisional; no external connection is asserted. Step290 begins a separate opposing-side assembly with a 3666/3020 plate pair and the 3023b/50340/77850/4032a support stack as shape candidates. Its 67142/68196 panel attachments are not placed until their branch contact is visible from later callouts. Steps291–292 add no physical instances: manual arrows show articulation of existing side panels, but exact pivot datums and target angles are unresolved; no candidate parts or alternate poses are counted as added inventory. Step293 shows the side-panel assembly on the fossil flank, but no mating point or axis; triceratops-base-289/290 remain independent local subassemblies pending connector evidence. Step294 plaque/minifigure are excluded and add no instances. Step250 adds one 3710 plate in a local fragment, long axis along the depicted body beam. The actual stud row, overlap and torso transform are unverified. Step251 adds three 11458 shape candidates and one 54200 slope candidate to a separate local fragment. Their shared placement is a callout layout only; exact contact, facing and torso transform remain unverified. Step252 50950 candidate rotated 90 degrees over the three 11458 candidates; 60x20 LDU footprint spans their 20-LDU pitch with nominal zero footprint residual. This is shape/pitch registration, not mold identification or insertion validation. Steps253–254: each 3023b pair is modeled beneath a 4032a round-plate candidate. 3023b stud centers at x=±10, z=10 align with a row of 4032a underside sockets at 20-LDU pitch; round plate bottom face is at y=0 after an 8-LDU offset. The central axlehole passes along local Y and remains unused/open. These are local fits only; the body attachment transform is deferred. Step289/290 50340 candidate DAT hinge axes were checked: each current identity transform preserves local +Z and the part-defined centerline y=2, finger-center span z=-16..+16 (32 LDU). Steps291–292 confirm panel articulation qualitatively, but do not identify the mating knuckles, pivot co-location, engagement depth or final angle; no transform was invented. Step252 vertical check: official 50950 bottom datum y=24 at instance y=-24 reaches y=0, matching the 11458 top datum y=0 for nominal 0-LDU face gap. This does not verify stud/recess engagement depth. Official 4032a comparison uses the central axlehol3/axlehol2 geometry, four peripheral studs and 8-LDU plate body. 18674 has a center stud instead of an open center hole; 30000 is a 2x2 brick with side pins and 24-LDU body. Both are worse fits to the enlarged callout, but no printed mold ID is visible. Steps256–258 are represented as a local two-arm L fragment. The 1x4 plate count/footprints are called out; the right-angle arrangement is diagram-based. Step257/258 plate reinforcement positions and 54200 facing are provisional. The 255 joint that ties the arms and the final body transform remain unresolved. Official 54200 bottom datum y=0 is positioned at y=8 to meet the 3023b top datum y=8 in step258; this height contact is provisional because the part identity/facing is candidate-level. Step259 2736 candidate axle axis is local X and is rotated onto 6541 +Z hole in -Z direction. The official 17.5-LDU shaft enters the 20-LDU hole 17.5 LDU, leaving 2.5 LDU to the far face; the ball center remains 12 LDU outside the near face. This is a geometry-fit candidate, not printed ID confirmation. 32000 and 54200 remain provisional upper placements; unclear round spacers are not double-counted.","catalog_and_asset_references":"official LDraw parts 32140, 32184, 98989, 11214 inspected; GoBricks SKU mappings remain unverified","full_connection_graph":"Step278 11214 pair is consumed internally between 32184 and the two connected 32140 holes. The remaining 32140 hole is the provisional torso-side port because step279 docks the completed link to the anterior torso; the 32184 orthogonal crosshole is the provisional skull-side port. These port-role assignments follow assembly order but remain subject to exact contact-part confirmation. A torso receiver is not required to satisfy both axes. The 247 single-hole candidate has 0 LDU transverse axis residual and 0 LDU face gap to the 32140 port; this is coordinate registration only. Step249’s paired support remains a candidate and its connection role/transform is unresolved. Printed p158 step293 supports only the qualitative flank association of the 289–292 panels; the hidden interface does not establish a connector, axis, insertion length or numeric assembly transform. Printed p159 step294 plaque and minifigure remain outside scope. Side-panel fold candidate: the official 50340 DAT carries a +Z hinge axis with fingers at z=±16. In the current independent 289/290 fragments each hinge candidate retains local +Z. The 291–292 arrows establish movement, not the exact mating part or angle.","exact_mesh_collision":"unverified_open_surface_probe_ambiguous","physical_build":"not_tested","mesh_collision_note":"A Blender Boolean probe was attempted after recursively triangulating LDraw DAT references. The flattened 32140 mesh retained 148 non-manifold edges of 2762; 32184 retained 360/2170; 11214 retained 383/1378; 6541 retained 56/520. Intersection volumes were nonzero small artifacts even for intended face contacts, so these booleans cannot establish collision-free fit. Use only the independently computed hole-axis/face-spacing checks until watertight solid reconstruction is available. The later step249 candidate probe likewise showed intersecting triangles at intended pin/receiver, joiner/pin and plate/brick interfaces; no valid solid-overlap result was produced.","surface_collision_note":"Open-triangle BVH tests were run on unmodified official LDraw meshes after the initial 278 link and again on the step249 candidate support. The 249 test reported intersections/zero nearest-surface distance at 6541↔43093, 43093↔62462, plate↔brick, and adjacent brick contacts. This watertightness-independent surface check cannot distinguish intended contact/friction engagement from penetration and cannot test containment. Result is ambiguous/unverified, not a collision-free pass. Keep separate from closed-solid Boolean probes, which were invalidated by non-manifold input.","open_questions":[{"id":"step247-small-round-parts","status":"deferred_user_uncertain_keep_candidates","manual_page":136,"step":247,"candidates":["6577.dat Technic Bush 1/2 Type 2","43093.dat Technic Axle Pin with Friction"],"evidence":"P136 exploded callout shows two small ring-like parts in a vertical stack below a 6541 candidate. 6577 has a female axle bore and fits the ring silhouette but requires an underlying shaft; 43093 has a male friction-pin form that can enter the 6541 side hole but is inconsistent with the depicted vertical spacer placement. Full product inventory thumbnails on printed pages 161–162 were checked against the two-item callout and surrounding assembly. The inventory prints LEGO element numbers rather than LDraw mold numbers; its small round connector thumbnails do not distinguish the concealed female axle bore from a protruding male pin at this view, so it narrows quantity/appearance but does not resolve 6577 vs 43093.","needed":"Already answered unclear/retain candidates. Do not ask again; revisit only if later assembly views expose the end profile or an independently verified element-to-mold mapping."},{"id":"step249-receiver-axis","status":"deferred_user_uncertain_keep_candidates","manual_page":137,"step":249,"candidates":["parallel 6541 hole axes","orthogonal 6541 hole axes"],"evidence":"The user asked to retain both orientations while uncertain. 32184 is provisionally skull-side and the remaining 32140 port torso-side, so the torso receiver need not align to both link axes. Parallel/orthogonal comparison alone does not eliminate either receiver candidate. The complete inventory thumbnail pages (printed 161–162) and page137 step249 callout were cross-checked; element-number-only inventory plus the obscured rear face does not establish the second 6541 axis. Port-role evidence from steps278–279 means this axis comparison cannot alone exclude a receiver candidate.","needed":"Already answered unclear/retain candidates. Do not ask again; use a later reverse-side or direct mating view if it appears."}]},"nodes":{"skull-torso-link":{"origin":"Link-local datum is the 92907 split-block origin. The top-level X=6800 is only an isolation offset.","step278_parts":["32056.dat","92907.dat","61332.dat x2"],"withdrawn_assumptions":["32140/32184/11214 identities","40-LDU old port pitch","shared +Y hole axis","+20 LDU old mating translation","step247 6541 receiver fit"],"verified_local_geometry":{"liftarm_hole_centers":[[0,0,0],[0,0,20]],"crossblock_port_lines":[{"point":[0,20,0],"axis":[1,0,0]},{"point":[0,20,-20],"axis":[1,0,0]}],"liftarm_transform":{"translation":[25,20,0],"matrix":[0,1,0,1,0,0,0,0,-1]},"pin_axis":[1,0,0],"pin_positions":[[20,20,0],[20,20,-20]],"pin_span_each":[0,40],"crossblock_x_span":[0,20],"liftarm_x_span":[20,30],"nominal_pin_insertion_into_liftarm":10,"pin_interface_status":"Hole centerlines and face datum match; 61332 section compatibility with one 32056 axlehol4 and one round peghole is not independently proven."},"current_status":"Step278 local hole axes, face registration and candidate pin span recomputed from current official DATs; local linkage is geometrically registered. Step279 counterpart is still unidentified: verified step247 47905/6141 and step249 6541/6141/25264 candidates do not yet expose a confirmed male port to mate with the crossblock +Z receiver."},"independent-base-280":{"origin":"local datum at center of 2x10 plate, isolated at world X=600 to keep it independent from torso/skull fragments","parts":[{"id":"part-0052","part":"3832.dat","role":"2x10 tan base plate; shape/stud count confirmed"},{"id":"part-0053","part":"50340.dat","role":"1x2 dual-finger hinge shape candidate; direction provisional"},{"id":"part-0054","part":"3623.dat","role":"first 1x3 plate, adjacent base row; placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0055","part":"3623.dat","role":"second 1x3 plate, adjacent base row; placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0056","part":"87079.dat","role":"step282 2x4 tile cover candidate; placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0057","part":"3023b.dat","role":"step283 1x2 plate row; position provisional"},{"id":"part-0058","part":"3700.dat","role":"step283 1x2 Technic brick with two holes; row/orientation provisional"},{"id":"part-0059","part":"50340.dat","role":"step283 first dual-finger hinge candidate; direction provisional"},{"id":"part-0060","part":"50340.dat","role":"step283 second dual-finger hinge candidate; direction provisional"},{"id":"part-0061","part":"3021.dat","role":"step284 2x3 plate; identity supported by six-stud callout and official shape, placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0062","part":"3022.dat","role":"step284 2x2 plate; identity supported by four-stud callout/underside and official shape, placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0063","part":"1762.dat","role":"step285 first of two 2x2 double-curved slope candidates; shape/quantity candidate, transform provisional"},{"id":"part-0064","part":"1762.dat","role":"step285 second double-curved slope candidate; paired row provisional"},{"id":"part-0065","part":"30355.dat","role":"step286 large studded triangular wing panel; official 6x12 left shape candidate, side/hinge transform provisional"},{"id":"part-0066","part":"30356.dat","role":"step286 mirrored 6x12 right wing panel candidate; exact callout mold allocation and hinge transform provisional"},{"id":"part-0067","part":"67142.dat","role":"step287 left 5x13 curved perforated panel candidate; outer edge registration provisional"},{"id":"part-0068","part":"68196.dat","role":"step287 right 5x13 curved perforated panel candidate; mirrored fit and hole engagement provisional"},{"id":"part-0069","part":"24299.dat","role":"step288 one of the counted pair on corresponding side; official handed wing shape candidate, precise contact provisional"},{"id":"part-0070","part":"24299.dat","role":"step288 one of the counted pair on corresponding side; official handed wing shape candidate, precise contact provisional"},{"id":"part-0071","part":"24307.dat","role":"step288 one of the counted pair on corresponding side; official handed wing shape candidate, precise contact provisional"},{"id":"part-0072","part":"24307.dat","role":"step288 one of the counted pair on corresponding side; official handed wing shape candidate, precise contact provisional"}],"status":"independent subassembly draft; steps 280–288 represented; outer wedge positions remain provisional"},"base-extension-289-local":{"origin":"center datum of the brown 3666 1x6 plate; independent step289 plate pair, held at world X=900 until its attachment point on the main base is measured","parts":[{"id":"part-0073","part":"3666.dat","role":"step289 brown 1x6 base; six-stud row confirmed by callout"},{"id":"part-0074","part":"3020.dat","role":"step289 tan 2x4 cap; four studs align to one row of 3666, row offset provisional"},{"id":"part-0075","part":"3023b.dat","role":"Printed p155 step289 callout: tan 1x2 plate by two-stud count. Placed at the free end of the local 3666/3020 pair; row/overlap provisional."},{"id":"part-0076","part":"50340.dat","role":"Printed p155 step289 callout: 1x2 modified hinge plate candidate. Local branch placement follows the successive substep, but finger direction and connection surface are provisional. Official DAT axis candidate +Z at y=2; step291–292 movement supports articulation but exact engagement/fold angle is unresolved."},{"id":"part-0077","part":"77850.dat","role":"Printed p155 step289: rounded-end reddish-brown 1x3 plate candidate, based on three-stud icon. Placed above the hinge area; exact part identity and row are provisional."},{"id":"part-0078","part":"4032a.dat","role":"Printed p155 step289 final callout: round tan 2x2 plate candidate, aligned above the brown round-end element. Center-hole identity and exact vertical layer remain unverified."}],"status":"steps289 substeps 1–5 represented locally; panel-to-base contact and final platform transform unverified","hinge_axis_check":{"part_candidate":"50340.dat","local_axis":[0,0,1],"local_axis_line_point":[0,2,0],"finger_centers_z":[-16,16],"current_instance_rotation":"identity; local +Z preserved","manual_evidence":"steps291–292 show adjacent panels rotating about the hinge row","status":"axis candidate registered; mating half/knuckles, pivot co-location, insertion and final angle unverified"}},"base-extension-290-local":{"origin":"center of brown 3666 1x6 local plate; separate branch on the opposing platform side, world X=1200 only as isolation placement","parts":[{"id":"part-0079","part":"3666.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290: six-stud reddish-brown 1x6 plate, local datum for opposite extension branch."},{"id":"part-0080","part":"3020.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290: eight-stud tan 2x4 plate aligned to one 3666 stud row; exact row offset diagram-based."},{"id":"part-0081","part":"3023b.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290: tan 1x2 plate candidate at the branch tip; local attachment row provisional."},{"id":"part-0082","part":"50340.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290 modified hinge plate shape candidate; finger direction and contact surface provisional. Official DAT axis candidate +Z at y=2; step291–292 movement supports articulation but exact engagement/fold angle is unresolved."},{"id":"part-0083","part":"77850.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290 three-stud rounded-end reddish-brown plate candidate, placed in the illustrated hinge stack provisionally."},{"id":"part-0084","part":"4032a.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290 round 2x2 plate/cap candidate on the local hinge stack; bore identity and depth unresolved."}],"status":"partial local subassembly; step290 perforated left/right panels are held only at their unresolved branch contacts while the plate/hook base proceeds","hinge_axis_check":{"part_candidate":"50340.dat","local_axis":[0,0,1],"local_axis_line_point":[0,2,0],"finger_centers_z":[-16,16],"current_instance_rotation":"identity; local +Z preserved","manual_evidence":"steps291–292 show adjacent panels rotating about the hinge row","status":"axis candidate registered; mating half/knuckles, pivot co-location, insertion and final angle unverified"}},"torso-extension-250-local":{"origin":"center of official 3710 plate; long axis local X, kept independent from body receiver until the stud row is visible","root_transform_status":"diagram-matched local extension; root X=1600 is only an isolation coordinate; body contact transform unresolved"},"torso-detail-251-local":{"origin":"center of the small step251 callout grouping, isolated from the torso and step250 fragment","root_transform_status":"callout silhouette/count placed locally; part facing, pin/peghole assignment and body transform remain provisional pending step252/253 and opposite-side views","step252":{"part":"50950.dat","position":[0,-24,10],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"evidence":"3x1 footprint and 11458 20-LDU stud pitch align after a quarter turn","status":"shape registration provisional; mold identity/insertion unverified","vertical_datum":{"50950_dat_bottom_y":24,"instance_y":-24,"resulting_bottom_y":0,"11458_top_datum_y":0,"nominal_face_gap_ldu":0,"status":"height registration checked; stud/recess engagement depth and mold identity unverified"}}},"torso-side-253-local":{"origin":"center axis of the 4032a 2x2 round plate; local +Y is the through axlehole axis","root_transform_status":"confirmed internal stud-pitch registration to 3023b; external torso-side placement and facing unresolved"},"torso-side-254-local":{"origin":"center axis of the second 4032a candidate; same internal interface as step253","root_transform_status":"internal pair registered; opposite-side transform is deferred because the view-turn icon does not encode a part transform"},"torso-rib-256-local":{"origin":"right-angle intersection datum of the two 3710 plates; fragment isolated at root X=2400","root_transform_status":"steps256–258 have a diagram-based local L layout; step255 corner subassembly remains unplaced, and neither inter-arm locking nor body transform is asserted"},"torso-detail-259-local":{"origin":"6541 hole-center datum; local +Z is the transverse hole axis and +Y is vertical","root_transform_status":"side 2736 candidate axis and span fit are registered; top brick/stud row is diagram-based; spacer stack withheld pending part identification"},"step247-249-candidate-review":{"step247":{"parts":["47905.dat","6141.dat","6141.dat"],"supersedes":["6541.dat","6577.dat","6577.dat"],"basis":"6649865.pdf p.136 callout; two black round plates stack below the black brick with opposite-side studs.","status":"shape and callout consistent; local stack heights follow 8-LDU plate DAT spacing; receiving contact remains provisional."},"step249":{"parts":["3023b.dat x2","6541.dat x2","6141.dat x2","25264.dat x2"],"core_registration":"Two 6541 at x=+/-10,y=-24 sandwiched between 3023b layers y=0 and -32, matching 24-LDU brick height plus 8-LDU plate cap.","6141_contact":"Each 6141 stud base coincides with one outward +Z 6541 hole center; 6141 local stud axis -Y is mapped to -Z. Center residual 0 LDU; contact identity remains a shape candidate because the manual shows shape classes, not mold IDs.","25264_contact":"Outer cap position/orientation is diagram-led only; receiving geometry and insertion are unverified.","status":"Core layer geometry registered; side-disc axis/center computed; outer cap and transform to torso receiver remain provisional."}},"early-display-steps-4-10":{"scope_correction":"Steps 4-10 are display-base/rock-and-plant assembly, not fossil skull construction.","step4":{"part":"18980.dat","color":"Dark Tan / LDraw 28","replaces":"50950.dat","placement":"18980 stud row aligned to base-end row x=40..140,z=±10; green 60474 round platform is one plate layer above. Exact page-11 contact remains provisional."},"step5":{"parts":["24316.dat x2","32064a.dat x2","3713.dat x2 shown in this local callout"],"replaces":["4519.dat and 2780.dat candidates"],"geometry":"32064a DAT local hole center [0,10,10], local axis -Z. Its transform maps center to [50,-38,0]/[110,-38,0] and axis to world -X. 24316 local shaft axis +X is antiparallel on the same centerline; 3713 local bore +Y maps +X.","rechecked_but_retained":["3700.dat step-3 technic bricks remain in the earlier assembly; 32064a.dat is a separate step-5 addition."]},"st